126	// insn gets an exec callback (icount-mode cost class): the tick ARMS on the
127	// ROI exit boundary (EXIT marker match, or vaddr == exit_pc) and DRAINS on
128	// the next callback. Exec callbacks fire before their insn executes, so the
129	// armed drain captures "after the boundary insn retired" -- exactly vsim's
130	// exit-drain record (DPC = next insn to execute) -- and reports that next
